From 08c7fd24f618157b726d8617f112bdca26cb3517 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 22:50:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] zed: add the Zeo application icon

Two PNGs, 512 and 1024, rendered from the SVG in the zeo repository's brand/
directory by brand/build-icon.py. The mark is CONSTRUCTED rather than traced -
every polygon comes out of a crystal model in that script - so it is reproducible
from source and is original work, not derived from Zed's trademarked mark. That
distinction is the point: neither the GPL-3 nor the Apache-2.0 grants any right
to Zed Industries' marks, so a rebrand that borrows the artwork is the one thing
that would actually create a legal problem.

sha256 of app-icon-zeo.png is ca89f90edc28c2a8..., matching brand/checksums.txt.
Do not verify against the archived checksums-antes.txt: that file records
72648be8..., the 204 KB placeholder this 34 KB render replaced, and a blind
`sha256sum -c` against it would "repair" the mark back to the version it retired.

Why the art is its own patch, ahead of the channel patch that uses it:

  crates/zed/src/zed.rs reaches the icon through include_bytes!, which is
  resolved at compile time. The file must exist in the tree before the About
  window can name it, so the two cannot be one commit without the art decision
  being baked into the channel work.

  THE DELIVERY OF THIS PATCH IS UNRESOLVED, and it is a trap worth naming.
  A binary hunk survives `git apply` and survives verify.sh, but refresh.sh
  regenerates every diff with

      git -C "${tree}" diff --cached --no-renames HEAD

  and no --binary. Without that flag git emits "Binary files a/x and b/x differ",
  a marker with no content - so the first bump after this lands would silently
  replace a working patch with one that cannot be applied, and nothing would
  report it until someone tried to build. Either refresh.sh gains --binary, or
  the ebuild copies the art in from FILESDIR and this patch is dropped from the
  series. Isolating the art here is what keeps that choice to one file.
